Media parsers
-------------
The container parsers in src/media (ISO BMFF, RIFF/WAVE, Ogg, MPEG audio / ID3) are original Rakvor code
written for this tool from the public format descriptions (ISO/IEC 14496-12, QuickTime File Format,
Microsoft RIFF/WAVE, EBU Tech 3285 BWF, RFC 3533 Ogg, RFC 7845 Opus, Xiph Vorbis I, ISO/IEC 11172-3 and
13818-3, id3.org ID3v2.3/2.4). No FFmpeg, libav or other GPL/LGPL/AGPL code or library is used or linked.
Worker isolation uses libc (MIT OR Apache-2.0) on Unix and windows-sys (MIT OR Apache-2.0) on Windows.

Sample evidence
---------------
Every file under examples/sample/evidence and examples/sample/reference is synthetic. It was generated byte by
byte by tests/make_samples.py (Python standard library only; deterministic) and is part of this project under the
same licence. The audio is a 440 Hz sine tone or filler bytes: no recording, no voice, no person. Product names
that appear inside the samples (Lavf, Audacity, Adobe Premiere, online-audio-converter.com, LAME, libopus,
libVorbis, com.apple.quicktime keys) are plain strings written to exercise the encoder classification; none of
those products produced the files. examples/sample/expected_findings.json and expected_hashes.csv are written
by the same script (hashes with Python hashlib and blake3).
